{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"According to the Mean Value Theorem, there exists a number $c$ in the open interval $4\u003cx\u003c13$ such that $h'(c)$ is equal to the average rate of change of $h$ over the interval:\n\n$h'(c)=\\dfrac{h(13)-h(4)}{(13)-(4)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"First, let's find that average rate of change:\n\n$\\dfrac{h(13)-h(4)}{(13)-(4)}=\\dfrac{6-3}{9}=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{3}}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now, let's differentiate $h$ and find the $x$-value for which $h'(x)=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{3}}$.\n\n$h'(x)=\\dfrac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x-3}}$ [[☃ explanation 1]]\n\nThe solution of $h'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{3}$ is $x=7.75$.  [[☃ explanation 2]]\n\n$x=7.75$ is indeed within the interval $4\u003cx\u003c13$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nh'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sqrt{3x-3}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(3x-3)^{\\large\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}(3x-3)^{\\large -\\frac{1}{2}}\\dfrac{d}{dx}(3x-3)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{3x-3}}(3)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x-3}}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"explanation 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nh'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{3}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{3}{2\\sqrt{3x-3}}\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{3}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\sqrt{3x-3}\u0026=\\dfrac92\n\\\\\\\\\n(\\sqrt{3x-3})^2\u0026=\\left(\\dfrac92\\right)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n3x-3\u0026=\\dfrac{81}{4}\n\\\\\\\\\n3x\u0026=\\dfrac{93}{4}\n\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=7.75\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $c=7.75$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $h(x)=\\sqrt{3x-3}$ and let $c$ be the number that satisfies the Mean Value Theorem for $h$ on the interval $4\\leq x\\leq13$.\n\n**What is $c$ ?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$5.25$","correct":false},{"content":"$7.5$","correct":false},{"content":"$7.75$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$11.5$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
